# EventPulse API

EventPulse is a backend API for discovering events, registering as an attendee, and receiving real-time announcements from event organizers. It handles authentication, event management, capacity-safe registrations, and live WebSocket-based announcements — built as a complete production-style Node.js backend from authentication through deployment.

## Tech Stack

- Node.js & Express
- MongoDB & Mongoose
- Socket.io (real-time announcements)
- JSON Web Tokens (authentication)
- express-validator (input validation)
- Jest & Supertest (unit and integration testing)
- Swagger / OpenAPI (API documentation)
- Vercel (deployment)

## Steps to Run the Project

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/doaasoliman733/EYOUTH-30906240105466-EventPulse.git
cd EYOUTH-30906240105466-EventPulse
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
npm install
```

Create a `.env` file in the project root (see `.env.example` for the required variable names):